1
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,220
Man, I'm wasting away over here.

2
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,017
After we visit my bro's grave, Dave,

3
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,377
what do you say we find a
place to get something to eat?

4
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:33,578
I'm good, but don't let me stop you.

5
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,637
Says here there's a new Italian
restaurant, and it's just up the road.

6
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:41,697
Wait, isn't that where the cemetery is?

7
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,957
Not the best place for a restaurant,
or anything for that matter.

8
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:45,920
Oh, Josuke,

9
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:50,557
this is just the kind of wacky food destination
that brings people in from all over.

10
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:51,860
It's to die for!

11
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,617
My mouth won't stop watering!

12
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,497
Or whatever it is the Fats
say, I just want to go.

13
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:58,521
Come on, Josuke, what do you say?

14
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:00,760
This is it?

15
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:03,179
I thought this building was vacant.

16
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,892
Maybe they remodeled it.

17
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,420
It sure has character.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:08,830
Huh?

19
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,080
That's weird.

20
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:12,180
What's diner dependent mean?

21
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:22,180
I'm digging the vibe
this place has going on.

22
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,030
Benvenuto.

23
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:30,400
Two today?

24
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:33,120
Here, please feel free to have a seat.

25
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,320
Oh, don't mind if I do.

26
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:39,200
Here you go.

27
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,680
Uh, right.

28
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,740
So chef, you a foreigner or what?

29
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,200
Si, signore.

30
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,120
I am originally from Italy.

31
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:50,900
My name is Tonio Trendi,
but you can call me Tonio.

32
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:52,549
This is the best day ever!

33
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:55,137
I finally get to eat
authentic Italian food!

34
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:58,102
My role as a chef has
taken me to many countries.

35
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,857
I've used the flavors
of my homeland and fused

36
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:03,437
them with the best culinary
traditions in the world.

37
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:07,108
Now I've made my way to Japan
in search of new opportunities.

38
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:10,060
Your Mariah is such a magnificent town.

39
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,869
You can find several farms with
many kinds of fresh produce.

40
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:15,921
Its fruity de mari are great too.

41
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,380
I adore it here.

42
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,497
Using Morio's wonderful ingredients,

43
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:24,197
I plan to make you a meal that will tickle
the taste buds and delight your senses.

44
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,110
Well, all right then.

45
00:02:25,193 --> 00:02:26,317
What do you think I should order?

46
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,700
Actually, I'll choose after
you show us the menu. Menu?

47
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:34,160
I'm sorry, but we don't use those. Huh?

48
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,377
What are you talking about?

49
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,837
What kind of restaurant doesn't use menus?

50
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,537
What I serve depends on
the patron I'm serving.

51
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,237
Well, you're serving
me, and I want the menu.

52
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,320
That won't do.

53
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:47,617
First, I have to examine the customer.

54
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,557
Then I decide what to prepare for them.

55
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,897
You've got to be kidding!

56
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:54,897
You don't let your customers choose
what they want to eat for themselves?

57
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:55,810
Alright.

58
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:57,660
Let's see now.

59
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,468
You had diarrhea yesterday.

60
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,340
Your intestinal walls are inflamed.

61
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,877
And it's obvious you're sleep deprived.

62
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,440
Yes, you only got four hours last night.

63
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:11,033
Which of course explains the puffy eyes.

64
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,346
Now let's see your left hand.

65
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:17,531
Your right foot is infected with a fungus.

66
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:20,817
You also have two cavities and
your left shoulder is stiff, yes?

67
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,730
What?

68
00:03:21,813 --> 00:03:23,177
How the hell did you know all that?

69
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,957
Everything you said
was right on the money!

70
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:27,580
It's all in the hands, amigo mio.

71
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:30,213
They are like a window into your health.

72
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,960
Oh, please excuse me.

73
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:37,056
And what will you be having, signore?

74
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,040
Oh, I'm not all that hungry.

75
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,006
But I'll take a cup of
coffee if you have any.

76
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,580
Make it a cappuccino.

77
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,260
Ho Capt, signore.

78
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:50,757
This guy can talk up his fancy
dishes as much as he wants.

79
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,437
Healthy food tastes like dog shit.

80
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,757
If it's even a little disgusting,
we don't have to pay for it.

81
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,317
We can just complain and leave.

82
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,230
Roger.

83
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:03,760
Hey, Josuke, this water!

84
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:07,100
No wait, it has to be
mineral water. What about it?

85
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:11,957
I've never been as totally sure about
something as I am right this moment.

86
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,687
This is the best water
that I've ever tasted!

87
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:18,690
Amazing!

88
00:04:18,773 --> 00:04:20,516
It's overflowing with sophistication!

89
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,337
It's like something a
mountain princess playing a

90
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:25,857
harp would drink as she
strums a beautiful melody!

91
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,757
It's wonderfully fresh and smooth!

92
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:32,781
Like the glorious first taste of water after
wandering in the desert for three days!

93
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:36,360
Wow! Yeah! You weren't
joking! It's amazing!

94
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:42,290
Divine!

95
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,090
You're right!

96
00:04:44,173 --> 00:04:45,003
It's first-rate!

97
00:04:45,086 --> 00:04:47,897
I wonder if they'll tell us
what brand of water it is?

98
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:48,810
You know,

99
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,257
this water's so good, I think I'm actually
going to shed a few tears over it.

100
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:54,170
Come on.

101
00:04:54,253 --> 00:04:57,717
A little sip of water isn't worth
weeping over no matter how good it is.

102
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,360
It must be its purity.

103
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:01,780
Do you have a handkerchief on you?

104
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:04,200
The waterworks are in full force.

105
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:08,480
The tears just keep coming.

106
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,641
They won't stop.

107
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,060
Okuyasu, you're acting weird, man.

108
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:14,240
Are you okay?

109
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,420
What the? Okuyasu! Holy shit!

110
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,657
What the hell is going
on with these tears?

111
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:22,681
They just keep pouring out of me!

112
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,150
Hey! Okuyasu!

113
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,257
I don't want to freak you out even more,

114
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:30,399
but the white parts of your eyes
are getting all shriveled and loose!

115
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:32,290
Momento.

116
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:33,800
Please try to remain calm.

117
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,240
You bastard!

118
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:37,994
The hell did you give Okuyasu to drink?

119
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,958
Tranquilo, signore.

120
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:42,437
His eyes have only been
temporarily withered.

121
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:45,617
He had 50,000-year-old
mineral water made from

122
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:48,537
melted snow procured from
Mount Kilimanjaro in Africa.

123
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:52,217
It flushes the ice interior
of harmful contaminants and

124
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:55,594
is an effective treatment in
cases of sleep deprivation.

125
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:59,057
The reason you didn't cry
after drinking the water is

126
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:02,669
because you obtained an adequate
amount of sleep last night.

127
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,090
Josuke!

128
00:06:04,173 --> 00:06:05,440
I'm not sleepy anymore!

129
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:08,317
To be perfectly honest with
you, I feel spectacular!

130
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:10,357
Like I slept a full ten hours!

131
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,820
Wait a second!

132
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,235
You can't be serious!

133
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:16,217
Are you telling me there's
nothing wrong with your eyes?

134
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,130
Exactly!

135
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,937
When you drink water this good, it's
only natural for the tears to flow.

136
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:23,377
Trust me, Josuke, it's
nothing to be worried about.

137
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:26,437
I cried way more than this
when I watched Champ on video.

138
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,177
Thanks for Karen, but I
feel like a billion yen!

139
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:30,360
Is that a fact?

140
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,220
You bet your ass it is.

141
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,080
Here's your cappuccino.

142
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:37,710
Oh, thanks.

143
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,900
So, shall we continue
with the next course?

144
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,820
Wow, looks grum-diddly-yumptious.

145
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:49,240
For our antipasto, I've prepared
insalata caprese with mozzarella.

146
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,740
Excuse me, but what's Masazo?

147
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:54,557
Goodness, you've never
heard of mozzarella before.

148
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,405
It's a soft, low-fat
cheese that's quite tasty.

149
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:00,080
It is a national favorite in Italy.

150
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:04,217
The first people to use tomatoes as a
culinary ingredient were the Italians.

151
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:08,737
The Italian people lead the entire world
when it comes to tomato based cuisine.

152
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:09,940
I'm not bragging.

153
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,077
It's the honest truth.

154
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,820
We take pride in our work

155
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:17,020
Now I hope you enjoy
your meal sir. Trust me.

156
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:17,990
I will

157
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:33,717
Well this dish is pretty
good I'll give you that I

158
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:38,337
dare say this is very good
but even so the cheese itself

159
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:41,437
doesn't leave much of an
impression which is a shame after

160
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:45,640
all the hype no no it's not
meant to be eaten by itself,

161
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,160
you have to add tomato to it. Say what?

162
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,106
Adding a tomato sounds weird.

163
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:53,497
Well, all right, but here in
Japan, we have sensitive palates.

164
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:57,168
This is gonna have to be
mind-blowing to pass the tasty test.

165
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:58,530
Um.

166
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:01,320
Oh my God!

167
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:08,857
It's incredible how the tomatoey nectar
gently caresses the fresh, delicate cheese.

168
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:10,411
What a great combination.

169
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,417
The cheese and tomato enrich each other.

170
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,237
It's a perfect symphony, I tell you.

171
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:19,660
A harmony of tantalizing flavors, A dynamic
duo the likes of Simon and Garfunkel!

172
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,647
or even Abbott and Costello.

173
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,557
It's like the writer-illustrator
team Osuo Takamori

174
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:28,240
and Tetsuya Chiba from the
comic Ashta no Joe! Crazy.

175
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,597
Nothing makes me happier than
knowing you enjoyed my cooking.

176
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,077
Hey, old buddy, old pal.

177
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:35,357
You think you can share some
of that with your bestie?

178
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,440
Not on your life.

179
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:39,229
You can order your own
as a salad, Konichi.

180
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:41,697
You're not getting any
of mine, you got that?

181
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:43,197
Even if you were starving to death,

182
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:46,633
I still wouldn't give you a
piece of this yummy goodness!

183
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,100
So good!

184
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:59,437
Everything I've been through has been
worth it to get beat at this moment!

185
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:00,350
Dick!

186
00:09:00,433 --> 00:09:03,717
I knew you were a stingy son of a
bitch, but this takes it to a new level!

187
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,660
Alright, fine.

188
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,194
I will have the same thing he's having.

189
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:08,870
Pocopito.

190
00:09:08,953 --> 00:09:09,900
That said,

191
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,917
the only one getting his
stiff shoulder corrected

192
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,882
today will be the gentleman
sitting to your left.

193
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:17,910
Huh?

194
00:09:17,993 --> 00:09:18,823
Stiff shoulder?

195
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:20,540
But you know,

196
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:23,597
I am starting to get a little
bit hot under the collar,

197
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,739
and for some reason I'm all sweaty.

198
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,060
Signore, might I humbly
suggest you remove your jacket.

199
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,757
What the hell?

200
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,080
Why am I so itchy all of a sudden?

201
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,600
What's going on?

202
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:46,757
What's all this flaky stuff
sticking to my fingers?

203
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:47,670
Semplice.

204
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:49,820
It's dead skin. Dead skin!

205
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:55,104
This is proof that we've greatly improved
your metabolic function and circulation.

206
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,790
The calcium,

207
00:09:56,873 --> 00:09:59,177
vitamins and minerals of the
antipasto have stimulated

208
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:02,142
your thyroid and its
metabolic hormone secretion.

209
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:05,337
The harmful cells are being
expelled as dead skin,

210
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:08,537
which is why you've been overcome
with an itching sensation.

211
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:10,040
Molto Bone, signore.

212
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,577
Keep scratching like that.

213
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:15,895
Because at the rate you're going, the
dead skin will be gone in no time.

214
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:22,790
Okuyasu!

215
00:10:22,873 --> 00:10:24,117
Come on, man, you have to cut it out!

216
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:26,157
This dead skin's the size of a softball!

217
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,946
We're digging into your
shoulder's muscle now!

218
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,130
No!

219
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:32,080
You're wrong, Josuke!

220
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:35,120
I'm so limber!

221
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,777
My shoulder's crazy flexible now!

222
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:41,507
Wow, it's so springy and light,
it's almost like I'm floating!

223
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:46,857
Check it out, my shoulders have never been
supple enough to bend around like this!

224
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:49,705
It's almost like I don't
have any bones at all!

225
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:52,880
The stiffness I had is good and gone!

226
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:59,577
If you'll excuse me, I'll be
heading back to the kitchen.

227
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:04,307
That pasta isn't going to get up and
serve itself while we stand here and chat.

228
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,800
He's amazing!

229
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,557
Actually, he's incredible!

230
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,875
We should come here to eat more often!

231
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,757
I don't think so.

232
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:18,040
This is getting way too freaky.

233
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:21,929
There is something seriously
weird about this guy's cooking.

234
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:31,160
Now, shall we continue with the next dish?

235
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,080
This is the primo piatto.

236
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:34,697
Today is pasta.

237
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:37,740
Spaghetti alla puttanesca.

238
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,660
Known as horse pasta,

239
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:44,724
this dish supposedly originated with
prostitutes who favored its easy preparation.

240
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:48,217
While cheese is not usually added
to pasta prepared with garlic,

241
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:50,380
this dish is a notable exception.

242
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:55,440
This spaghetti, am I crazy or
does it have chili flakes in it?

243
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:56,854
An astute observation.

244
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:59,857
This special sauce used
in spaghetti puttanesca is

245
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:02,940
one of the oldest recipes
found in Italian cuisine.

246
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:07,796
And not to brag, but my hometown,
Napoli, is considered its birthplace.

247
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:11,568
So, of course, I give it the
highest possible recommendation.

248
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:13,677
You should have said that earlier.

249
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,348
I can't eat anything spicy.

250
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:18,197
The only kind of curry
rice I can handle is that

251
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,097
mild Vermont curry that
has apples and honey in it.

252
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,121
Oh, and don't get me started
on wasabi with sushi.

253
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,280
I can't do it! It's too spicy!

254
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,680
It's like eating fire!

255
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:32,520
There's a simple solution, then. Ready?

256
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,300
Don't eat it.

257
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:42,102
If it's not to your liking,
don't force yourself.

258
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:45,497
I'd be more than happy to
remove the pasta from your bill.

259
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:47,977
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'll prepare the main course.

260
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:50,697
I hope the secondo piato
will suit you better.

261
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:52,237
But so you know, signore,

262
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:54,597
I make my spaghetti to
be enjoyed even by those

263
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:57,386
who have the lowest
tolerance for spicy foods.

264
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:02,952
So I can eat this even though it's spicy?

265
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,250
Hot!

266
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,380
I know Tonio's a master chef.

267
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:08,617
Anybody with taste buds would agree.

268
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:11,577
And if you ask me, I'd even
say the guy's a genius.

269
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,697
But this really wasn't his best work.

270
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:17,015
No, I think you lucked out
with your spice intolerance.

271
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,250
Huh?

272
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:21,877
Hasn't it crossed your mind that this food
and water might be a little too weird?

273
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:22,977
Something's shady.

274
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:24,589
What do you mean by shady?

275
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:25,910
Spicy?

276
00:13:25,993 --> 00:13:28,657
You scratched off a
softball-sized wad of dead skin,

277
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,977
and that's after you
cried a freaking river.

278
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,140
I guess I did.

279
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:35,157
But that time I went to
Shirabu Onsen in Yamagata,

280
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,357
I lost even more dead
skin than I did today?

281
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,737
and my back got better.

282
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:40,585
It's totally normal, isn't it?

283
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,030
Hot!

284
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:43,010
Listen!

285
00:13:43,093 --> 00:13:46,617
Remember what I said about that little
chat with Hazamada in the hospital?

286
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:50,137
I don't know why, but it
seems that stand users...

287
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:53,317
He said stand users are
inadvertently drawn to each other.

288
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:57,540
Josuke, are you really trying to
tell me Tonio's a stand user? Shh!

289
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:02,780
We can't say for sure yet, which is why
I chose the word shady. Got it. Shady.

290
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:05,180
Oh, come on!

291
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,380
Why is it so hot?

292
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:08,077
If you can't handle spicy food,

293
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:10,557
maybe you should quit trying to
stuff it in your mouth already.

294
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:11,470
You're right.

295
00:14:11,553 --> 00:14:13,107
I should just give up on it.

296
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:16,200
Spicy food and meat don't
mix at all. That's true.

297
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:20,106
But for some reason, I can't stop
tasting this delicious sauce.

298
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:27,632
Why are you eating that?

299
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,937
Yeah, it's weird, right?

300
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,137
I wouldn't usually be able to
chow down on anything just spicy.

301
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:33,050
But now...

302
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:36,080
I can't stop!

303
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:39,657
After that first bite, the
spice bit back and won't let go!

304
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:42,297
It's like eating your weight
in beans during a festival.

305
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:45,957
And even though they don't taste good,
before you know it, you've eaten a whole bag!

306
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,697
And you don't regret a damn thing,

307
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,780
because all you can feel
is your body wanting more!

308
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,812
Hey, I told you to stop eating that crap!

309
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:00,257
I can't explain it, but
I'm getting even hungrier!

310
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:03,928
The more spaghetti I ate, the
more that I want to scarf down!

311
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,630
Tasty!

312
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:08,600
Okuyasu, calm down!

313
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:15,140
Holy shit! Your tooth!

314
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,812
That's the cavity I had!

315
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,744
The rotten tooth just fell out!

316
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:29,880
Actually, I think one of the
bottom teeth had a cavity, too. Ah!

317
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,120
I was right, another rotten tooth.

318
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,460
Whoa, a new molar is already growing in.

319
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:53,760
I've had enough of this.

320
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:56,697
Time to find out what that
chef from hell's planning.

321
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:58,160
Do it, Shining Diamond!

322
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,960
But I wasn't done with that!

323
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,533
Sorry to ruin the meal,

324
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:11,346
but I'm reverting the ingredients
back to their original forms!

325
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:27,497
Hey, what in the world were
those little things, Josuke?

326
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:28,420
It's a stand.

327
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:30,760
So my hunch was right after all.

328
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,887
Tony Otrendy's a stand user.

329
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,494
Okuyasu, are you okay?

330
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,740
My sleepiness is finally gone.

331
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,480
My stiffness melted away.

332
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:44,377
And my cavities were replaced.

333
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:46,680
But my stomach hurts.

334
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:50,420
I've never felt such
excruciating pain in my life!

335
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,980
Hang on! Tonio!

336
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,456
What the hell are you trying to pull?

337
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:07,240
Where is he?

338
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,800
So he's already finished our main course.

339
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,070
Excelente.

340
00:17:28,153 --> 00:17:29,680
I want you to enjoy it.

341
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:35,162
Judging from this, it appears my main dish
of lamb with apple relish was a success.

342
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,590
Quiet!

343
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,857
What exactly do you think
you're doing back here?

344
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,300
Did you see?

345
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,497
Answer the question, per favore!

346
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,815
Did you enter my kitchen to spy on me?

347
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,600
Now prepare yourself, signore!

348
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,560
You're going to pay dearly!

349
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,957
Give me one good reason
why I should stand here and

350
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:09,217
listen to you hurl around
threats about making me pay!

351
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,517
I should threaten you!

352
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:14,365
Now, what the hell are you trying
to do with that food of yours?

353
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:20,207
Okuyasu, wait a sec,
what are you eating now?

354
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:24,320
I can't stand it, my stomach
hurts, but I can't stop eating.

355
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:27,517
A tangy sweet apple relish
combined with juice from

356
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:31,060
the lambs makes every
single morsel pure ecstasy.

357
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,680
Who knew food could taste
this finger licking good?

358
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:37,119
For the love of God, drop the meat.

359
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,160
This is the best day ever.

360
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,301
It's like a waterfall of
pleasure washing over me.

361
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:43,930
Amazing.

362
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,730
What?

363
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,180
My guts fell out!

364
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:55,640
My stomach's dying!

365
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:00,720
Uncle Yasu!

366
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:06,540
I'm putting an end to this!

367
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,840
Oh no!

368
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:12,362
Wash your disgusting hands
with softness instant!

369
00:19:14,780 --> 00:19:18,486
Honestly, entering a kitchen
without permission is inexcusable!

370
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:22,677
Ascolti, cleanliness in the
kitchen is priority one, amico mio!

371
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,220
Wait, wash my hands?

372
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:26,126
You aren't trying to kill me?

373
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:27,697
Hey, Josuke!

374
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:30,309
It's like my insides
have been rejuvenated!

375
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:34,226
Not only that, I'm completely
full and feel as fit as a fiddle!

376
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:37,880
And best of all, my diarrhea
tummy's all better! What?

377
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:41,617
Oh my, that's wonderful to hear!

378
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:45,477
I love knowing that my cooking brought
happiness and health to a customer.

379
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:46,637
Believe me when I tell you,

380
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:48,097
there's no greater sense of joy and

381
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:51,180
accomplishment for me than
nurturing a hungry soul.

382
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:53,570
The puppy!

383
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:58,077
With such unconventional flavors,
I wanted him to taste testy.

384
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:01,557
Our furry friend here was having
a bit of a digestive problem, too.

385
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:05,400
So, you mean, you just wanted
Okuyasu to eat a good meal?

386
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,960
You don't have ulterior motives? Hmm?

387
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:11,777
What else could a chef want from a
patron but for them to enjoy the food?

388
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:13,757
The thought gets me out
of bed in the morning.

389
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:15,797
It's everything I could ever hope for.

390
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:18,056
And to be clear, you're a stand user.

391
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,600
We have them too.

392
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,370
Oh!

393
00:20:23,453 --> 00:20:24,560
I can't believe my eyes!

394
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:26,960
Where to start?

395
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:30,597
A while back I was traveling the
world in search of the perfect cuisine

396
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:34,457
when out of the blue I discovered
I had these fantastical powers.

397
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:38,997
Never in my wildest dreams would I have
thought I'd meet others similar to myself.

398
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:40,820
Even so, that's no excuse!

399
00:20:41,060 --> 00:20:42,777
You have to possess common sense!

400
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:45,977
You touched my kitchen without
washing your filthy hands!

401
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:47,577
If I was cross with you earlier,

402
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:50,957
it's because I'm aware that the
kitchen's worst enemy is germs!

403
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:51,870
What?

404
00:20:51,953 --> 00:20:53,060
Oh, I'm sorry.

405
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,037
That didn't even cross my mind.

406
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:57,473
I hope you're ready to put in some work.

407
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:59,860
Now, shall we continue the cookie?

408
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:04,740
Dessert is... pudding?

409
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,330
Ha!

410
00:21:06,413 --> 00:21:07,906
I'm too manly for this stuff.

411
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:11,297
Well, I'll eat it, but it
doesn't mean I'm gonna like it.

412
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,210
I'll...

413
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:13,797
Oh, my God!

414
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,420
You really are a genius!

415
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,680
You are amazing!

416
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:20,100
A brilliant artist! Yeah, yeah.

417
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,960
Yuck it up, Okuyasu.

418
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,671
It sounds as though he's enjoying dessert.

419
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:26,930
Hmm?

420
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:29,137
This kitchen isn't going to scrub itself!

421
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:31,440
Oh man, this is the worst!

422
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:33,540
My athlete's foot is gone!

423
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:36,880
I shall await your return, my new friends.

424
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,440
Molte Crazy.

425
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,940
Unless I'm mistaken, you're Jotaro Kujo.

426
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,219
I'm with the Speedwagon Foundation.

427
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:05,817
Until you hear otherwise,

428
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:09,417
any electrical wiring including
phone lines poses a threat

429
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:12,617
and that's why I've come to
deliver this message in person.

430
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:18,740
At noon tomorrow I expect to
arrive in the port of Morioh.

431
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:26,080
Joseph Joestar

432
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,417
Anytime I need to see a
face, it has closed my eyes.

433
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:56,677
And I am taken to a place
with a crystal mind.

434
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:59,457
A magenta feeling, take a
shelter in the face of my spine.

435
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:00,857
Straight like a Chaka cherry cola.

436
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:03,457
I don't need to try to
explain, I just hold on tight.

437
00:23:03,540 --> 00:23:05,797
And if it happens again,
I'ma move so slightly.

438
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,417
To the arms and the lips and the face.

439
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:10,017
To the human kind of all
that I need to, I want to.

440
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:12,237
Come and stand a little bit closer.

441
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,517
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

442
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:18,957
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you.

443
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:23,260
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you.

444
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:26,380
Ooh, I got to find you.

445
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:32,260
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you.

446
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:35,600
Ooh, I got to find you.
